WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.210
Varys: Though the Targaryens had forged the
Seven Kingdoms in fire and blood, they didn't

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.200
govern with them.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.720
Until they did.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:15.670
Maegor, First of His Name, defined counsel
as confirmation and disagreement as treason.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.390
Three Grand Maesters tried to avert disaster.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:23.699
Instead of taking their advice, Maegor took
their heads.

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:28.380
As a second son and exile, Maegor was never
meant to rule.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.700
But no sooner did Maegor hear of his brother's
death that he flew Balerion to Dragonstone

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.600
and demanded the crown.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.320
Only the Grand Maester dared object that the
throne should pass to his older brother's

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.860
firstborn son, Prince Aegon.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:46.890
Maegor insisted that the Iron Throne should
go to the man with the strength to seize it,

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.940
and beheaded the Grand Maester.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.079
Prince Aegon soon took him at his word.

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:58.030
He claimed his father's dragon, raised a host
of Westermen, and marched on King's Landing

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.760
while Maegor was in Oldtown.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.530
Far from the capital, Maegor couldn't rally
an army to match Aegon's.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:09.600
So he ordered his banners to swarm Aegon's
larger army from all sides, confusing the

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.340
young prince and slowing his advance.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:18.340
Beneath the Gods Eye, Maegor's disparate forces
came together and attacked Aegon as Maegor

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.240
himself swooped down from the clouds.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:26.000
For the first time since the Doom of Valyria,
dragon fought dragon in the sky.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.950
But Aegon's dragon was no match for Balerion
the Dread, who was four times its size.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:35.920
When Aegon fell to his death, his army broke
and fled.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.460
For slaying his own nephew, Maegor forever
after became known as "The Cruel."

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.159
Though, of course, not to his face.

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:50.310
The next Grand Maester dared object to Maegor
taking a third wife when taking his second

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:55.020
wife had ruined his brother's reign because
Maegor's first wife was the niece of the High

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.590
Septon.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.859
But Maegor beheaded the Grand Maester and
declared war on the Faith.

00:02:00.859 --> 00:02:06.189
He set fire to the Riverlands, the Westerlands,
and the Reach in a campaign to root out disloyal

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:10.380
lords and sponsored a more pliant High Septon.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.310
None of it worked.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:16.220
Maegor may have returned to the capital with
two thousand skulls of the Faith Militant,

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.070
but most of them weren't soldiers.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:23.670
They were simple folk who had sheltered the
outlaw septons or turned out in droves to

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.570
hear them denounce the wicked king.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:32.050
The third Grand Maester dared to declare Maegor
the father of his own heir.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:38.580
But when his second wife miscarried, and Maegor
saw the monstrous stillbirth, Maegor beheaded

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.510
the Grand Maester for his insolent adherence
to truth.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:48.200
So he had no one to warn him when his third
wife, sensing an advantage, declared that

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:53.490
his second wife had been unfaithful, and produced
a list of potential fathers of the misshapen

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.010
child.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:59.970
Not only did Maegor execute his second wife
and her father, his own Hand of the King,

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:04.820
but he also marched on her family's castle
and slaughtered everyone who bore a drop of

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.960
her family's blood.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.820
But his third wife couldn't give him a child
either.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:16.240
Desperate to cement his stolen throne with
an heir, Maegor took three wives at once,

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:21.030
known as the Black Brides because each were
women he'd widowed in his wars.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:27.850
All three women grew full with child in time,
but each gave birth to the same twisted monstrosities

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.850
as his second wife.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:35.540
One need not be a maester, much less a Grand
Maester, to deduce the common thread here.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:41.180
Though Maegor stamped out the fires of rebellion,
his cruelty and fear only scattered more tinder

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:45.710
over the realm until even the smallest ember
could set the realm alight.

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:51.360
One day, the Faith Militant emerged from the
shadows, and the lords sent to quash it joined

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.819
it instead.

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:56.030
His Hand resigned and retired to his island
home.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:04:01.319
Finally, House Baratheon declared for Maegor's
own nephew as the rightful king.

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:07.350
The Lannisters, Tyrells, and Arryns soon joined,
adding more than half the might of Westeros

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.110
to the prince and his two dragons.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:15.700
Which became three when Maegor's niece and
involuntary Black Bride stole away from the

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.519
Red Keep with her dragon.

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:20.010
Her treason wasn't even the last.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:24.090
Maegor's own lord admiral sailed the Royal
Fleet into his nephew's harbor.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:29.840
But most fitting of all, when Maegor tried
to send ravens to call his banners, he found

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:36.190
that his fourth Grand Maester had learned
from his predecessors and fled.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.840
Maegor spent one final night on the Iron Throne.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:45.660
He was found in the morning with his wrists
slashed and one of the throne's blades jutting

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.150
from his throat.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:52.610
Nobody knows if it was one of his queens or
Kingsguard or one of the thousands who wanted

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:53.610
him dead.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:58.790
Or even Maegor himself, frustrated that his
body had failed his will.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:02.980
Whoever the culprit, no doubt he died as all
tyrants do.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.660
Believing that history would vindicate him.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.620
It hasn't.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:12.810
History may be written with fire and blood,
but histories aren't.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:16.650
As any good advisor could have warned him.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:22.380
The coin of Aerys, Second of His Name, had
landed on madness.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.130
But half the coins of the Targaryens had landed
so.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:32.860
Yet only Aerys would be known as the Mad King,
thanks, in no small part, to the Defiance

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.990
of Duskendale.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:40.950
Duskendale was the greatest port on Blackwater
Bay until Aegon built King's Landing.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:47.940
As the capital grew richer and more prosperous,
it sucked ships and gold away from Duskendale.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:54.690
To halt its long decline, the Lord of Duskendale,
Ser Denys Darklyn, petitioned King Aerys for

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:59.530
a royal charter that would allow him to levy
his own port fees and taxes, which would obviously

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:02.650
be lower than in King's Landing.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:06.610
The Hand of the King, Tywin Lannister, refused.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:11.250
But knowing of the tension between the Hand
and its king, Ser Denys invited the king to

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:17.120
Duskendale to evaluate his petition himself
rather than deferring to his Hand.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:23.240
When Tywin admonished the king to refuse,
as any sensible advisor would, a petulant

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:29.270
and bristling Aerys instead accepted, traveling
to Duskendale with a small retinue and only

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.810
one of his Kingsguard.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:37.480
As soon as Aerys stepped within the city,
Ser Denys seized him, killing the Kingsguard

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:40.699
and the few others who dared to defend their
king.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:46.180
Aerys was hauled to the dungeons to have his
beard pulled and have other petty cruelties

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:49.620
inflicted on his royal person.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:54.520
Lord Tywin immediately raised an army and
marched on Duskendale, but Ser Denys threatened

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:58.130
to kill the king at the first signs of an
assault.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:03.340
If Ser Denys hoped to force Tywin to offer
terms, he didn't know Lord Tywin, who refused

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:08.030
to even parley until Ser Denys released the
king and surrendered.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:12.790
The royal army surrounded the city, and the
royal navy blockaded it.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:17.389
Ser Denys had clearly not anticipated such
obstinacy.

00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:22.479
Nor that the king's Hand would be in no rush
to save the maddening king, when, as Lord

00:07:22.479 --> 00:07:27.870
Tywin himself pointed out, the realm had a
better option in the king's much more stable

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:30.300
son, Prince Rhaegar.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.210
After six months, Lord Tywin's patience was
at an end.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:39.919
Or, at least, none could claim he acted recklessly
if he now stormed the city, and Ser Denys

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:41.229
killed the king.

00:07:41.229 --> 00:07:46.260
But the dutiful and honorable Ser Barristan
the Bold volunteered to infiltrate the city

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:51.410
and rescue his king single-handedly, as befit
his Kingsguard oath.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:59.280
Tywin couldn't refuse such valor publicly
and so begrudged Ser Barristan one night.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:04.520
Then he would storm the city and put every
man, woman, and child to the sword.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:11.060
With only his hands, Ser Barristan climbed
the city walls in the dark of night and snuck

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:16.000
through the city disguised as a beggar, evading
patrols and suspicious townspeople.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:22.540
When he reached the walls of the city keep,
the Dun Fort, he scaled those by hand as well,

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:26.419
even dispatching the wall guard before he
could sound an alarm.

00:08:26.419 --> 00:08:32.229
With incredible bravery and luck, Ser Barristan
made his way to the dungeons and freed his

00:08:32.229 --> 00:08:33.599
king.

00:08:33.599 --> 00:08:35.969
Then Ser Barristan's luck ran out.

00:08:35.969 --> 00:08:38.039
A cry went up through the castle.

00:08:38.039 --> 00:08:40.440
Someone had discovered the king was gone.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:46.200
With horns and trumpets blaring an alarm,
Ser Barristan cut their way to the stables,

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:50.990
avenging his slain Kingsguard brother but
taking an arrow to his chest.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:56.110
Slipping through the castle gate just as it
closed, the wounded Ser Barristan and Aerys

00:08:56.110 --> 00:09:01.130
rode through the roused town, racing for the
city walls and, beyond it, the safety of the

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:03.080
royal army.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:08.430
Lord Tywin's archers raced forward to clear
the walls of defenders, and Ser Barristan

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:14.860
the Bold earned immortality by delivering
King Aerys to the waiting, if not welcoming,

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.190
arms of his Hand.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:23.860
Without his hostage, Ser Denys surrendered
and begged mercy from the same king he'd imprisoned.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.410
Most men would have had none.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:27.610
Aerys had less.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:34.410
He commanded Ser Denys be executed along with
man, woman, or child who bore his family name

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:36.740
and anyone who once had.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:42.830
As for Ser Denys's foreign wife, who had urged
his defiance, Aerys commanded that her tongue

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:46.710
and womanly parts be torn out, and she be
burned alive.

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:51.380
It was his first time passing such a sentence.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:54.620
It must have given him a taste for it.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:10:00.020
For the king rescued from Duskendale was not
the same king who'd entered it.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:05.380
Many men would crack after six months in a
dark cell, being mocked, prodded, and tweaked.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:07.910
Aerys had arrived cracked.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.110
Now he was shattered.

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:12.320
For years, he would refuse to leave the Red
Keep.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:17.940
Encouraged no doubt by his worried advisors,
since he also refused to allow any blades

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:22.750
near his person, even to shave his beard,
cut his hair, and trim his nails.

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:28.630
He began to see enemies in every shadow, who
vanished only when the fires burned.

